  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 AM EST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nLow level height field tightens today in response to a system \npassing off to the north with diurnal mixing supporting a few \nlate morning/afternoon westerly gusts up to 25-30 mph. This \nsystem does force a weak front through later today into tonight.\nNo threat for rain however given the dry column and overall \nweak ascent. Low amplitude west-northwest flow aloft persists \notherwise into Tuesday with quiet wx and gradual warming. \n\nA deep upper level trough remains on target to dig into the Eastern \nUS late Wednesday through Saturday with deepening northerly flow \nand colder temperatures. The last several model cycles have been \nfarther north with the leading wave and sfc reflection Wednesday \nafternoon-night with increasing prospects for a period of rain.\nThis low exits east into Thursday and Friday with colder \nnortherly flow in its wake. Rounds of mid level dpva and deep \nnortherly flow with 850 mb temps down to near -5C looking should\nsupport a healthy long lake axis response during this time into\nfar nw IN and possibly sw MI. The lake modified mixed layer \ncould cool just enough for the first snowflakes to mix in \nfurther inland later Thursday night.",
